  "worked_solution": "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v={210}^{\u2218},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-{210}^{\u2218}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{210}^{\u2218}+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{210}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
